    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d699">

                <pb facs="0920" n="808" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg808"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 412.00/58</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Fletcher</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-30T18:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 30, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1323. Your 1079, May 17, 1 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d699-f1"/> Department has
                    not received promised note from Foreign Office respecting claims commission. If
                    note has not yet come to you, ask Foreign Office when it may be expected, and
                    press for prompt and, if possible, satisfactory reply. Mexico could do much to
                    improve friendly relations with United States and promote good feeling among
                    injured Americans by establishment of strong, impartial claims commission, which
                    would win confidence and respect of claimants concerned.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d699-f1" n="1" xml:id="d699-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed. Reports that Foreign Office is preparing reply.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
